BT /F2 10 Tf 0.04 0.29 0.56 rg 49 570 Td (6. STATIC RECOGNITION - WHY 126 VALUES?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 548 Td (For the two-hand static pathway, each hand has 21 landmarks. Each landmark has three coordinates:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 536 Td (x, y, and z. One hand therefore has 21 x 3 = 63 values. Two hands have 2 x 21 x 3 = 126 values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 524 Td (The 126 values are the length of a feature vector. They are not 126 signs, 126 training samples,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 512 Td (or an accuracy score.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 500 Td (The current intended label metadata includes HELLO, I_LOVE_YOU, NO, THANK_YOU, and YES. The live) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 488 Td (backend status and actual model classes are authoritative for the deployed system. A label) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 476 Td (appearing in metadata alone does not prove that the class is recognised reliably.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 464 Td (Correct landmarks do not guarantee correct classification. Errors may arise from unfamiliar hand) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 452 Td (shapes, orientation, occlusion, missing hands, mismatched feature preparation, or visually similar) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 440 Td (classes.) Tj ET
q 0.86 0.92 0.98 rg 44 417 524 18 re f Q
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.04 0.29 0.56 rg 49 422 Td (7. SEQUENCE RECOGNITION - WHY TIME MATTERS) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 400 Td (A single frame captures a moment. Some signs depend on movement over time, so the project also has) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 388 Td (a sequence pathway. The sequence feature utility uses 132 values per frame: the 126 landmark) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 376 Td (coordinates plus six wrist-position values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 364 Td (The sequence is resampled into 10 time bins. The resulting input is 132 x 10 = 1,320 values.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 352 Td (This is the designed input format; it does not prove every continuous sign has been learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 340 Td (correctly. Performance depends on labelled sequences, order, segment boundaries, preprocessing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 328 Td (training quality, and testing on unseen examples.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 316 Td (For a judge: "Static recognition classifies features from a frame. Sequence recognition uses a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.12 0.16 0.21 rg 50 304 Td (time-ordered representation of multiple frames.") Tj ET
